1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,385
AI can outline every organoid in a microscope

2
00:00:02,435 --> 00:00:03,298
image in seconds.

3
00:00:03,348 --> 00:00:05,733
It also gets about one in five wrong,

4
00:00:05,783 --> 00:00:06,950
and never tells you.

5
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:07,807
This is VeriCell,

6
00:00:07,857 --> 00:00:10,664
built during the Meta AI Developer Hackathon on Muse Spark,

7
00:00:10,714 --> 00:00:12,950
SAM 3.1, Muse Voice and Muse Spark Open.

8
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:14,950
Microscopy AI that knows when it's wrong.

9
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,258
A scientist asks a plain question,

10
00:00:17,308 --> 00:00:19,181
out loud if they like:

11
00:00:19,231 --> 00:00:21,104
which organoid is the largest?

12
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,027
Muse Spark reads the image and turns the

13
00:00:33,077 --> 00:00:34,950
question into a strict plan.

14
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:37,642
SAM 3.1 and Cellpose-SAM outline 531 candidates,

15
00:00:37,692 --> 00:00:41,488
and SAM starts from words we measured it actually understands:

16
00:00:41,538 --> 00:00:43,796
the word 'organoid' alone finds nothing.

17
00:00:43,846 --> 00:00:47,258
Every candidate gets a calibrated chance of being real,

18
00:00:47,308 --> 00:00:49,181
and plain code measures everything.

19
00:00:49,231 --> 00:00:51,488
The model never invents a number.

20
00:00:51,538 --> 00:00:54,181
Then the agent decides what to double-check:

21
00:00:54,231 --> 00:00:57,258
Muse Spark judges two doubtful crops and hands

22
00:00:57,308 --> 00:00:58,796
them to the scientist.

23
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:03,412
The answer: 8,240 square pixels, with an honest range.

24
00:01:03,462 --> 00:01:07,258
But VeriCell also checks whether the conclusion itself could change.

25
00:01:07,308 --> 00:01:09,565
Organoid 321 is six percent bigger,

26
00:01:09,615 --> 00:01:12,642
and only fifty-nine percent likely to be real.

27
00:01:12,692 --> 00:01:14,950
If it is, it's the answer.

28
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:21,873
Say you want to publish:

29
00:01:21,923 --> 00:01:24,565
the largest organoid is at most 9,000.

30
00:01:24,615 --> 00:01:28,027
VeriCell stress-tests the claim. One organoid, thirty-six percent likely,

31
00:01:28,077 --> 00:01:29,181
would break it.

32
00:01:29,231 --> 00:01:32,258
This conclusion is one cell away from wrong.

33
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:38,412
So the scientist checks only the objects that matter.

34
00:01:38,462 --> 00:01:40,719
321 is real: the answer moves,

35
00:01:40,769 --> 00:01:43,412
and the table shows exactly what changed.

36
00:01:43,462 --> 00:01:46,104
The other three are debris. Four clicks,

37
00:01:46,154 --> 00:01:49,565
and the conclusion holds. Test the claim again: robust.

38
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:01,873
Against the hand-measured truth, 8,818,

39
00:02:01,923 --> 00:02:04,565
the checked answer is within one percent.

40
00:02:04,615 --> 00:02:07,642
Before the checks it was seven percent off.

41
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:13,412
It can tell a microscope where to look again,

42
00:02:13,462 --> 00:02:15,719
and export every decision as evidence.

43
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:17,873
This isn't one lucky image.

44
00:02:17,923 --> 00:02:19,796
On a sixty-eight-image organoid benchmark,

45
00:02:19,846 --> 00:02:23,642
VeriCell beats the published agent on all sixteen question types.

46
00:02:23,692 --> 00:02:25,181
Its warning means something:

47
00:02:25,231 --> 00:02:27,873
when it says a size conclusion holds,

48
00:02:27,923 --> 00:02:30,565
it's wrong thirteen percent of the time;

49
00:02:30,615 --> 00:02:32,104
when it warns, forty-nine.

50
00:02:32,154 --> 00:02:35,565
It spots wrong cells better than SAM's own confidence,

51
00:02:35,615 --> 00:02:37,873
with a calibration error of 0.012.

52
00:02:37,923 --> 00:02:41,335
And the whole reasoning layer runs on open weights,

53
00:02:41,385 --> 00:02:43,642
Muse Spark Open, with matching results.

54
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:46,873
AI that measures is easy.

55
00:02:46,923 --> 00:02:49,950
AI that knows when it might be wrong,

56
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:53,027
and helps a scientist find out, is VeriCell.

57
00:02:53,077 --> 00:02:54,181
Try it live.
